 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519571,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Arthur buys a house. Their 15-year mortgage comes to $225,879 with 4.91% interest. If Arthur pays off the mortgage over those 15 years, how much will they have paid in total?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In the previous exercise, you found the monthly payment was $949.72.</p>\n<p>The total paid, <i>T</i>, on a <i>t</i> year mortgage with monthly payments <i>pmt</i> is <i><span data-math=\"T = pmt \\times 12 \\times t\"></span></i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"T = {\\text{ }}979.72{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}12{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}20{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}\\$319,620.60\"></span></p>\n<p>Arthur pays $319,620.60 in total.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$319,620.60"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
